<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arthur Cipriani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1875">1875</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arthur Cipriani was a Trinidadian soldier, labour leader and politician of Corsican descent. After serving in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> Workingmen's Association from 1923 and campaigned for self-government, workers' rights and universal suffrage. He was a long-serving mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-spain">Port of Spain</a> and member of the legislative council.</p></div>
